{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c37aae89b25cc853e7050b895fa86f7fec740e26d3ede4cf69bb187c5010e468","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI/CD integration test harness","key_entities":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","--max-worker-restart=0","loadgroup","--dist","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","dsession.py:555-568","loadscope.py:166-205","--timeout-method=thread"],"problem_keywords":["pytest","xdist","loadgroup","worker restart cascade","timeout","worker crash","integration test","loadscope"],"propositions":["When an xdist worker crashes or times out under loadgroup/loadscope, the pending workload including the crashing item is requeued, causing the respawned worker to re-run and crash again, cascading up to xdist's default restart cap (numprocesses*4) and consuming excessive CI time.","Setting --max-worker-restart=0 on the integration lane aborts the session immediately on worker crash instead of cascading respawns, serving as a guard to bound blast radius.","The loadgroup lane must carry --max-worker-restart=0 flag in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml to prevent worker restart cascades.","A contract test in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py must pin the --max-worker-restart=0 flag on the loadgroup lane to prevent silent regression."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787536190035053001,"uuid":"ba6fa850-e7fe-4eb2-93b1-748ba41c6695"}